08-0fce1486794c" :question/math-academy-id "q-41785" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -4 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix, $B$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix, and $C$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $2\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding $2$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $3\\times 2$ matrix, which will require finding $6$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $AB$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $AB$ by $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =(AB)C \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 15 \\\\ 3 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186115835 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c24ee771-dbe8-598f-84ff-60f041661edb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186113948} {:answer/id #uuid "31f22e55-3257-560c-9b8b-1a370672646f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186113949} {:answer/id #uuid "41fb8df9-f182-543a-ad39-bd4d9406f6c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186113950} {:answer/id #uuid "4c8e5b8a-9724-51db-b122-6afd0420a1df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186113951} {:answer/id #