& -21\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186264802} :answer-field/id #uuid "42ab1d01-3d95-5a64-a3f9-0807a0efbbe8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186265368}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e430effe-7959-580a-be3d-d4b5f50f0d27" :question/math-academy-id "q-130313" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, $B$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix, and $C$ is a $1\\times 3$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $3\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding $3$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $2\\times 3$ matrix, which will require finding $6$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $AB$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $AB$ by $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =(AB)C \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -3 & -9 \\\\ -8 & 8 & 24 \\\\ 7 & -7 & -21\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186292860 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62b9489d-1bd9-53ad-9584-412222a7fecf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id 17592186291053}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62b9489d-1bd9-53ad-9584-412222a7fecf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id 17592186291053} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a8b6a87-5f6a-54ec-bbe9-05756798dc46" :answer-field/key "fi