=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix, $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix, and $C$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $3\\times 2$ matrix, which will require finding $6$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $1\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding only $1$ entry.\n\nSo, we find the product $BC$ first: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-20-6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-26\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $A$ by $BC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =A(BC) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-26\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}78 \\\\ -52 \\\\ -182\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186299814 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6482cff8-ea84-5d14-a24d-9034a0c7b0a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id 17592186297981}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6482cff8-ea84-5d14-a24d-9034a0c7b0a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id 17592186297981} :answer-field/id #uuid "24506a77-9b74-5997-b750-9ae0f37f53de" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186298759} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4004e514-65cc-5ba3-8951-7fdfa32a9481" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-60" :db/id 17592186297805}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4004e514-65cc-5ba3-8951-7fdfa32a9481" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-60" :db/id 17592186297805} :answer-field/id #uuid "4fb3cc92-18ef-57d1-8cf8-4873a0f63452" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186298907} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67ac13fb-5f80-5b63-8caf-0023f6f87094" :