matrix, which will require finding $4$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $AB$ first: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 11\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $AB$ by $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =(AB)C \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 11\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186392501 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e619a67-9c5c-5198-a6e6-8fe2cae308d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}55 \\\\ -21 \\\\ 50\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186392503} {:answer/id #uuid "26af411f-4369-55ad-9e9b-e90514a5bcc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-68 \\\\ -22 \\\\ 50\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186392504} {:answer/id #uuid "d5580b66-a310-537c-a0c5-a20457678669" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-68 \\\\ -22 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186392505} {:answer/id #uuid "45d96025-8f3a-50af-9de9-cd071e5ec232" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}68 \\\\ -22 \\\\ 40\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186392506} {:answer/id #uuid "a3df1fc7-14b6-532e-b12c-6343f041272c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}42 \\\\ -12 \\\\ 50\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186392507}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26af411f-4369-55ad-9e9b-e90514a5bcc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-68 \\\\ -22 \\\\ 50\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186392504} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed3d0a23-eac0-554f-905e-6466f6601ed5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186392502}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4cbd1e16-e623-56fd-8563-e7c6cd4b5ff2" :question/math-academy-id "q-42258" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, $B$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix, and $C$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $3\\times 3$ matrix, which will require finding $9$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $2\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding $2$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $BC$ first: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $A$ by $BC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =A(BC) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-68 \\\\ -22 \\\\ 50\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186392508 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f0a43c89-29de-5118-a4d4-3f996c643cb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -2 \\\\ 15 & -7 \\\\ 9 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186392510} {:answer/id #uuid "c445d736-2b33-5a39-a7be-0a95976a8481" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 15 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186392511} {:answer/id #uuid "cbc16d9e-74fc-598e-a8df-a8298f3cced4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -2 \\\\ -15 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186392512} {:answer/id #uuid "b96c80d8-2ac1-5468-adbf-38acb2a30f63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186392513} {:answer/id #uuid "49f1aa56-0832-5de3-ba9b-9f00b6b7f69f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 15 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186392514}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49f1aa56-0832-5de3-ba9b-9f00b6b7f69f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 15 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186392514} :answer-field/id #uuid "c68e793c-51ab-520a-a8e9-a83467b6243d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186392509}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "72c2951d-d6a9-5cec-b270-d342a8fcfdc1" :question/math-academy-id "q-42259" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, $B$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix, and $C$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $3\\times 3$ matrix, which will require finding $9$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $2\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding $2$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $BC$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $A$ by $BC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =A(BC) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 15 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186408070 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4caef308-f829-5678-91b0-8c356246d3db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186408051} {:answer/id #uuid "5305f733-f1f5-5fee-a5d0-db365d37810d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-14 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186408052} {:answer/id #uuid "adb0e76d-9986-5b8e-a736-d4821798cae1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186408058} {:answer/id #uuid "efb8a5b6-21b1-5345-9b9e-e436922d4029" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186408063} {:answer/id #uuid "feae4636-ed31-53a4-b5a1-dfde035b20cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-14 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 28\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186408064}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "feae4636-ed31-53a4-b5a1-dfde035b20cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-14 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 28\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186408064} :answer-field/id #uuid "9eb9eed7-da79-5b44-8508-0e1881d8523f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186408066}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "38a55885-c791-5e66-b4d4-e155d750a7c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-130322" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, $B$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix, and $C$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $3\\times 3$ matrix, which will require finding $9$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $2\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding $2$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $BC$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $A$ by $BC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =A(BC) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-14 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 28\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186485578 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c8bceae-a8f8-59df-9913-53898f44b673" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id 17592186485052}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c8bceae-a8f8-59df-9913-53898f44b673" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id 17592186485052} :answer-field/id #uuid "16cf85a0-d4e0-503b-a40c-377068739a10" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186485376} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df658338-ffbc-54a4-8fc3-4233fa4b9c9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id 17592186485286}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df658338-ffbc-54a4-8fc3-4233fa4b9c9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id 17592186485286} :answer-field/id #uuid "91a5a09a-06e9-5e46-b927-635849a5367f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186485429} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3e847ec-d131-5985-94dc-25f91ed6df64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id 17592186485336}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3e847ec-d131-5985-94dc-25f91ed6df64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id 17592186485336} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc2e3df9-3029-583e-b5fd-63d9b4b790dc" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186485478}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c4c5958e-629a-595b-ba26-53d736ebe0b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-320017" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $ABC=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, $B$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix, and $C$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix. Therefore,\n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$ gives a $3\\times 3$ matrix, which would require finding $9$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$ gives a $2\\times 1$ matrix, which requires finding $2$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $BC$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $A$ by $BC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =A(BC) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -15 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Associative Law"}
